                           "Rivergate rose from the wet plain at noon, all gray walls, red roofs, and chimney smoke pressed low by rain. Gobolin had seen its towers in woodcuts. None had included the line of wagons stranded before the eastern gate or the pikes angled toward him when the patrol approached.",
