                           "The council chamber smelled of wool, wet cloaks, and old authority. Duchess Elira sat beneath Rivergate\u0027s green banner. She was young enough that every older councilor explained her own town to her and careful enough to let them finish. A narrow gold circlet rested above close-cropped brown hair. Whenever two councilors spoke over each other, she aligned the three ink bottles on the table before her.",
